<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <title>Calculator</title>
  <style>
    body {
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
    }

    .calculator {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
      grid-gap: 5px;
    }

    .calculator button {
      padding: 10px;
      margin: 0;
      border: none;
      border-radius: 5px;
      background-color: #4caf50;
      color: #fff;
    }

    .calculator button:hover {
      background-color: #388e3c;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <div class="calculator">
    <button id="7">7</button>
    <button id="8">8</button>
    <button id="9">9</button>
    <button id="+">+</button>

    <button id="4">4</button>
    <button id="5">5</button>
    <button id="6">6</button>
    <button id="-">-</button>

    <button id="1">1</button>
    <button id="2">2</button>
    <button id="3">3</button>
    <button id="*">*</button>

    <button id="0">0</button>
    <button id=".">.</button>
    <button id="=">=</button>
    <button id="/">/</button>
  </div>

  <script>
    const buttons = document.querySelectorAll('.calculator button');
    const display = document.createElement('span');
    document.body.appendChild(display);

    buttons.forEach(button => {
      button.addEventListener('click', () => {
        display.textContent += button.textContent;
      });
    });

    document.querySelector('#=').addEventListener('click', () => {
      const result = display.textContent;
      display.textContent = eval(result);
    });
  </script>

</body>
</html>
```

**How it works:**

* The HTML code creates a basic calculator layout using a grid.
* The JavaScript code:
    * Queries all the buttons in the calculator.
    * Creates a variable `display` to store the current output.
    * Adds an event listener to each button that appends its text content to the `display` element.
    * Adds an event listener to the `=` button that evaluates the expression in the `display` element and displays the result.

